<section class="sg-sec" id="listen"><h2>Listen</h2><div class="sg-video" data-yt="FUuQwcQZQqo" data-title="Palästinalied (Palestine Song): Origo Ensemble"><button type="button" class="sg-play"><span class="sg-play-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sg-play-t">Play the performance</span><span class="sg-play-n">Origo Ensemble</span></button></div><p class="sg-video-cr">On YouTube, from the channel Origo Ensemble. Pressing play loads YouTube&#8217;s player. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FUuQwcQZQqo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on YouTube<span aria-hidden="true"> &#8599;</span></a></p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Alte clamat Epicurus (Carmina Burana, CB 211)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">c. 1230</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (the Palästinalied's first stanza is added to it as CB 211a)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">All die Weil Ich Mag (Ougenweide)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1974</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (recording)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Congregatio (Corvus Corax)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1991</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (recording)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Qntal II (Qntal)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1995</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (recording)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Crusaders (Estampie)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1996</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (recording)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Weckt die Toten! (In Extremo)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1998</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (recording)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Undrentide (Mediaeval Baebes)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2000</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (recording)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Palästinalied-Projekt</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2002</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (compilation of 20 performances)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">String Quartet Set, first movement (Lou Harrison)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (takes much of its melody)</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lanquan li jorn (Jaufre Rudel)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">12th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (suggested contrafactum)</span></li></ul></section>
